---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Delete your identity and data"
  description="How to remove Identizen from a phone, revoke a device, and have the public index delete everything it holds about an identity."
>
  <div class="container-site max-w-3xl py-16 sm:py-24">
    <article class="prose-idz">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="mt-2 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Delete your identity and data</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-fg-muted">
        Identizen has no accounts, emails, or passwords. What exists is a key on your phone and a
        short record about that phone on the public index. Both can be removed by you, without
        asking anyone.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Remove the identity from a phone</h2>
      <p>
        In the app, open <strong>Settings</strong> and choose <strong>Forget this identity</strong>.
        The private key, recovery phrase, and activity history are erased from the phone
        immediately. Nothing about them was ever sent anywhere, so there is nothing else to delete
        for that part.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Revoke the phone on the index</h2>
      <p>
        Sign in to <a href="https://app.identizen.com">app.identizen.com</a> from another device, open
        <strong>Devices</strong>, and revoke the phone. From that moment the phone can no longer
        sign in anywhere, every browser it paired is unpaired, and every session it opened is signed
        out. The index marks the device record as revoked rather than deleting it, so that the
        revocation stays effective and can be audited; step 3 removes it.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Ask us to delete everything</h2>
      <p>
        To have the index remove every record tied to an identity, including device records,
        per-site identifiers, and the audit trail, use the <a href="/contact/">contact form</a> or write
        to <a href="mailto:privacy@identizen.com">privacy@identizen.com</a> and include the identifier
        shown on the app's Home tab (it begins with <code>idz_</code>). We confirm the request by
        sending a sign-in challenge to that identity, so only its holder can trigger it, and
        complete the deletion within 30 days. Hosting request logs, which contain IP addresses,
        expire on their own within days.
      </p>

      <h2>What is kept</h2>
      <p>
        Nothing that identifies you. After step 3 the index holds no record of the identity at all.
        Sites you signed in to keep whatever account they created for you under the per-site
        identifier; deleting that is between you and each site, since Identizen never sees it.
      </p>

      <p class="mt-8 text-sm text-fg-muted">
        See also the <a href="/legal/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> for what the index stores and why.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>
